# Copy to .env and adjust. Do not put secrets in this file.
#
# AGENT_MODE picks where the model comes from. Leave it unset and the agent
# guesses from whatever credentials it can see: the proxy if AIET_TOKEN and
# AIET_PROXY_URL are both set, then Gemini if GOOGLE_API_KEY is set, and
# Bedrock otherwise. Set it explicitly to be sure — the agent prints the mode
# it settled on at startup either way.
#
#   proxy    the interview proxy, Claude models, no AWS account needed
#   gemini   the Gemini API directly, with your own free API key
#   bedrock  Bedrock, with your own AWS credentials
#
# AGENT_MODE=proxy

# AGENT_MODEL overrides the model for whichever mode is in force, so its valid
# values differ per mode — see each section below. Every mode has a default, so
# you can leave it unset.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mode: proxy — no AWS account, no credentials.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The token is short-lived (1 hour) and is supplied to you separately — it does
# not belong in this file or in git. Export it instead:
#
#   export AIET_TOKEN=<the token you were given>
#
AIET_PROXY_URL=https://nbylnotlx5fcsdkawr3ntxfita0nhyrg.lambda-url.us-west-2.on.aws/

# One of: sonnet-5, sonnet-4.5, haiku-4.5. Defaults to sonnet-4.5. The proxy
# also caps output at 4096 tokens, request bodies at 32 KB, and allows 10
# requests per 60 seconds with one request in flight at a time.
# AGENT_MODEL=sonnet-4.5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mode: gemini — the Gemini API with your own key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. It is free, and the flash
# models have a free tier — but the free tier is rate limited per minute and
# per day, so a long conversation can run into 429s. GEMINI_API_KEY works too.
# A key is a secret: export it rather than committing it here.
#
#   export GOOGLE_API_KEY=<your key>
#
# Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash-lite. gemini-3.7-flash is the stronger (and
# still free-tier) option if the lite model struggles with the tool loop.
# AGENT_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mode: bedrock — your own AWS credentials.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials are NOT read from here. Bedrock uses the AWS SDK default provider
# chain (environment variables, AWS_PROFILE, SSO, or an instance role), and you
# need model access for the inference profile below.
#
# AGENT_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0

# Region to call Bedrock in. Falls back to AWS_REGION, then us-east-1.
# Ignored by the other modes.
# AGENT_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
